// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_POC_CYCLIC_LENGTH
// RUNTIME: exercise via `anubis run`.
// SILENT_WRONG closed: `anubis_cyclic` had `.max(0) as usize`, so a negative length silently
// became 0 and returned `[]`. A caller computing `cyclic(computed_len)` from broken arithmetic
// would see empty output and cyclic_find would report "not found", hiding the real bug behind
// a plausible-looking negative-space code path. Same shape as HKDF / PBKDF2 length fixes.
fn main() {
    print(cyclic(-5));
}
